3. What if the source is an EC2 instance inside a VPC?
A VPC does not contain an S3 bucket; S3 is a regional AWS service. Your EC2 instance can upload files to a bucket in another Region using AWS CLI or an SDK, provided the IAM permissions and network connectivity are configured.

For example:
aws s3 cp report.csv s3://destination-bucket/reports/report.csv \
  --region ap-south-1

Use an appropriate S3 VPC endpoint or other permitted network path. If the bucket is in another Region, make sure the CLI uses the destination Region. This command copies a file once; it does not establish continuous replication.

CRR vs CORS vs AWS Backup
Concept	Purpose
S3 CRR	Automatically replicate S3 objects to another Region
S3 cross-account access	Allow an authorized principal in another account to access bucket objects
CORS	Allow browser-based applications from specified origins to make cross-origin requests
AWS Backup cross-account copy	Keep recoverable backups in a separate account
AWS Backup cross-Region copy	Keep recoverable backups in another Region

Interview tip: If asked, “How would you copy S3 data from one Region to another automatically?”, answer S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR). If asked, “How would you protect EC2 and RDS backups against account compromise or regional outages?”, answer AWS Backup with cross-account and/or cross-Region copy, depending on the requirement.


